# Binaries
/bin/
/chronicle
*.exe

# Test and coverage output
*.test
*.out
coverage.*

# Local environment
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# Eval reports. `chronicle eval --json` writes the model's own reasoning about
# each memo, and a reason is ABOUT a transcript and will quote it — so a report
# from the `real` stratum is corpus-adjacent, and tier 2 does not go in git
# (CHRN-36 §1). Ignored so committing one needs a deliberate -f.
*.eval.json

# The web app (CHRN-53). node_modules is reproducible from web/bun.lock; the
# built bundle is reproducible from `bun run build` and is what deploy/
# Dockerfile's web stage produces before `go build` embeds it. Only the
# placeholder that makes //go:embed always resolve is checked in. `vite build`
# empties dist/ first, so the build script itself touches the placeholder
# back afterward — this ignore rule alone would not survive a build.
web/node_modules
web/dist/*
!web/dist/.gitkeep

# The Android client (CHRN-59). node_modules here is not an app dependency: it
# is the openapi-generator launcher that scripts/gen-dartapi.sh runs, plus the
# generator JAR it downloads on demand, both reproducible from mobile/bun.lock
# and mobile/openapitools.json. The generated Dart package under
# mobile/chronicle/packages/ IS committed, and CI byte-compares it against
# openapi.yaml -- same reasoning as internal/api/wire and web/src/api.
mobile/node_modules
